<ContentPage
  title="Accessibility Statement | SpedCentral"
  description="SpedCentral's commitment to digital accessibility for families and professionals of all abilities."
  heading="Accessibility Statement"
  lastUpdated="July 27, 2026"
>
  <p>
    SpedCentral serves families and professionals in the special education community -- which means accessibility
    isn't a nice-to-have for us, it's the point. We're committed to making spedcentral.com usable by everyone,
    including people who use assistive technology like screen readers, switch devices, or voice control.
  </p>

  <h2>Our standard</h2>
  <p>
    We aim to meet <strong>WCAG 2.1 Level AA</strong> (Web Content Accessibility Guidelines), the widely accepted
    standard for web accessibility, across the Site.
  </p>

  <h2>What we've built with this in mind</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Semantic HTML headings and landmarks so screen readers can navigate the page structure;</li>
    <li>Descriptive alt text on images;</li>
    <li>Color choices checked for sufficient contrast against text;</li>
    <li>A site that works without requiring JavaScript for core content to be readable.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Known limitations</h2>
  <p>
    Accessibility is an ongoing effort, not a one-time checklist. Some third-party content -- for example, an
    individual provider's own website that we link out to, or embedded product images from a manufacturer -- is
    outside our control and may not meet the same standard. We're also actively improving keyboard navigation and
    focus states across newer parts of the Site as we build them.
  </p>

  <h2>Feedback</h2>
  <p>
    If you encounter an accessibility barrier anywhere on SpedCentral, please tell us specifically what page and
    what happened -- email <a href="mailto:hello@spedcentral.com">hello@spedcentral.com</a>. We treat accessibility
    reports as a priority, not general feedback.
  </p>
</ContentPage>
